<title>NEW ZEALAND: HongkongBank says cuts NZ fixed rates.</title>
<headline>HongkongBank says cuts NZ fixed rates.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>HongkongBank said on Wednesday it had cut rates on its New Zealand fixed rate mortgage lending products by up to 0.75 percent.</p>
<p>The following cuts were made (percent) -</p>
<p>	     Old rate		   New Rate</p>
<p> 1 yr:	8.5			  8.2</p>
<p> 2 yr	 9.25			 8.6</p>
<p> 3 yr	 9.35			 8.6</p>
<p> 4 yr	 9.9			  9.25</p>
<p> 5 yr	 9.9			  9.25.</p>
<p>Manager of personal banking business, Alex Bentley, said the reductions were a direct result of falls in wholesale rates, particularly at the longer end of the curve.</p>
<p>&quot;Longer-term rates have stabilised at much lower levels in recent times allowing the bank to reduce its rates and pass on the benefits to prospective and new customers,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom +64 4 471 4273  </p>
<p>For further details of leading New Zealand banks' variable and fixed mortgage rates click on page  NZREN.</p>
</text>
